    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_6f25cde0",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: islam_is_a_religion_of_peace_if_you_dont_agree_then_youre_ignorant; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a group of men in an angry, confrontational protest, with one man in the foreground shouting and pointing aggressively while holding green flags. The overlaid text reads: 'islam is a religion of peace if you don't agree then you're ignorant.' This juxtaposition of an image of intense anger and aggression with a claim about Islam's peaceful nature is inherently contradictory and inflammatory. The meme uses the visual of rage to mock or undermine the claim that Islam is a religion of peace, implying that those who disagree are ignorant. This is a hateful intent because it attacks the beliefs of Muslims by equating disagreement with ignorance, and it uses the image of anger to delegitimize the peaceful nature of Islam. The meme is designed to provoke and incite hostility toward Muslims by framing their beliefs as irrational or ignorant, which is a direct attack on a protected characteristic (religion).",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a5f1cd89"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
